Create Group 01 — Interaction Controls for the DevKit.

This group is part of Layer 01 — Foundations & Interface Primitives.

Use the DevKit Core Design Constitution as the immutable global design foundation.

Do not redefine global colors, spacing, typography, breakpoints, radii, shadows, motion, accessibility, or responsive rules. Inherit them from the Core Design Constitution.

The purpose of this group is to provide the fundamental interactive action components used throughout the entire DevKit.

The group must contain exactly these 10 components:

001 Button
002 Icon Button
003 Button Group
004 Split Button
005 Link Button
006 Floating Action Button
007 Toggle Button
008 Segmented Control
009 Command Button
010 Action Menu Trigger

These must be genuinely reusable UI components.

Do not create page sections, dashboards, templates, cards, marketing blocks, or application-specific components.

Every component must be independently usable and composable with other DevKit components.

Each component must have:
- semantic HTML
- accessible interaction
- keyboard behavior
- pointer behavior
- touch behavior
- focus management
- screen-reader support
- loading state where applicable
- disabled state
- hover state where applicable
- pressed state
- selected state where applicable
- error state where applicable
- responsive behavior
- Light theme
- Dark theme
- High Contrast compatibility
- RTL support
- localization support
- reduced-motion support
- dynamic text scaling support

Use the exact DevKit spacing, typography, color, radius, elevation, icon, and motion tokens.

Never introduce arbitrary values.

Components must support:
XS
SM
MD
LG
XL

unless a specific component has a semantic reason not to support every size.

Default interactive control height should use the global 40px token.

Touch interaction must maintain at least a 44×44px effective hit target.

Components must visually distinguish:
default
hover
focus
pressed
disabled
loading
selected
success/error states where relevant.

Do not make every component visually identical.

Each component must have its own semantic interaction model while maintaining the same underlying design language.

Use one coherent icon system.

Icons must have meaningful semantic relationships with their actions.

Do not use decorative icons when they provide no useful information.

The components must work independently and in combination.

Test all components at:
Compact
Mobile
Tablet
Desktop
Large Desktop
Ultra Wide

The design must adapt rather than simply shrink.

On mobile:
- prioritize primary actions
- maintain touch targets
- prevent action overflow
- allow text wrapping where appropriate
- move secondary actions into appropriate menus when necessary

On desktop:
- support hover
- keyboard shortcuts where meaningful
- tooltips where appropriate
- richer action density
- pointer-specific behavior

Avoid excessive:
- gradients
- glass effects
- shadows
- borders
- animation
- rounded containers
- decorative elements

The group should feel premium, calm, precise, tactile, and exceptionally refined.

After implementation, test:
- long labels
- short labels
- icons only
- RTL
- localization
- disabled states
- loading states
- keyboard navigation
- screen readers
- touch
- high contrast
- reduced motion
- high zoom
- narrow mobile widths
- extremely wide desktop widths

Do not duplicate functionality between components.

Each component must have a clearly defined reason to exist.